From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Gomez <da.gomez@kernel.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] report: let XUNIT_TESTCASES name where the xunit testcases go

check collects each test's xunit <testcase> in a file under its private
$tmp and writes result.xml from it only when the section ends. When the
machine under test crashes or hangs mid-section, the run never reaches
that point, and the results of every test that finished are lost with
$tmp, although each one was complete.

When XUNIT_TESTCASES names a file, append the testcases there instead,
for example on storage that outlives the machine. Whoever runs check then
still has the finished tests' results after a crash, and can start check
again with the rest of the tests (-E naming those that ran): it appends
to the same file, and the result.xml it writes at the end holds the tests
of both runs. check never removes the file, so a fresh run must start
from an empty one, and it serves one section per run. Unset keeps the
previous behaviour.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Gomez <da.gomez@kernel.org>
---
 common/report | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/report b/common/report
index 2fa15e6..2c06fd1 100644
--- a/common/report
+++ b/common/report
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@ _xunit_make_section_report()
 	if [ $sect_name == '-no-sections-' ]; then
 		sect_name='global'
 	fi
-	local report=$tmp.report.xunit.$sect_name.xml
+	local report=${XUNIT_TESTCASES:-$tmp.report.xunit.$sect_name.xml}
 	rm -f "$tmp_fn"
 	# Header
 	echo "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>" > "$tmp_fn"
@@ -179,7 +179,7 @@ _xunit_make_testcase_report()
 	if [ $sect_name == '-no-sections-' ]; then
 		sect_name='global'
 	fi
-	local report=$tmp.report.xunit.$sect_name.xml
+	local report=${XUNIT_TESTCASES:-$tmp.report.xunit.$sect_name.xml}
 
 	echo -e "\t<testcase classname=\"xfstests.$sect_name\" name=\"$test_name\" time=\"$test_time\">" >> $report
 	case $test_status in
-- 
2.53.0

